      "created_at": "2020-07-12T18:38:32.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>To go with the default FengShui solution: Blowing things up helps with all sorts of problems. :)</p>\n<p>So I'll try an example:</p>\n<p>*As the stricken&nbsp;freightship noticably gained momentum towards the roaring abyss, CowboyX cocked his guns and gave his allies a grim nod. \"I'll buy us some time\" he grunted, disappearing into the engine deck.&nbsp;Moments later, one of the large engines rocketed away with a screeching sound, its recoil forcing the trembling vessel&nbsp;into a momentary standstill between the two forces.*</p>\n<p>I'm certainly no writer (and english isn't my first language either), but I still think this should sound&nbsp;familiar, in all its cheesiness. And we don't even get to know what CowboyX did there precisely.</p>\n<p>Of course, whatever players&nbsp;make up should make barely enough sense to get away with - but myself, I'd not set the bar too high. Comics are full of 'explanation' that defies all laws of real-life&nbsp;physics.</p>",
      "post_number": 8,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:06:19.990Z",
